<p dir=3D"auto">Redux can be described in three fundamental principles:</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>1. Single source of truth:</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p dir=3D"auto">The state of your whole application is stored in an object =
tree inside a single store.</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir=3D"auto">This makes it easy to create universal apps, as the state f=
rom your server can be serialized and hydrated into the client with no extr=
a coding effort. A single state tree also makes it easier to debug or inspe=
ct an application; it also enables you to persist your app's state in devel=
opment, for a faster development cycle.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
