<p dir=3D"auto">The single source of truth is our state tree, that is not r=
ewritten or reshaped. It gives us the availability to easily retrieve infor=
mation in constant time and maintain a clean structure for the state of our=
 application.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">In React-Redux applications, when your Redux is a single so=
urce of truth, it means that the only way to change your data in UI is to d=
ispatch redux action which will change state within redux reducer. And your=
 React components will watch this reducer and if that reducer changes, then=
 UI will change itself too. But never other way around, because Redux state=
 is single source of truth.</p>
<p align=3D"center" dir=3D"auto">
  <a target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" href=3D"https://github.c=
om/learning-zone/react-basics/blob/master/assets/redux-state.png"><img src=
=3D"https://github.com/learning-zone/react-basics/raw/master/assets/redux-s=
tate.png" alt=3D"Redux State" width=3D"500px" style=3D"max-width: 100%;"></=
a>
</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">A practical example would be that you have Redux store whic=
h contains items you want to display. In order to change list of items to b=
e displayed, you don't change this data anywhere else other than store. And=
 if that is changed, everything else related to it, should change as well.<=
/p>
