<p dir=3D"auto">There is no "right" answer for this. Some users prefer to k=
eep every single piece of data in Redux, to maintain a fully serializable a=
nd controlled version of their application at all times. Others prefer to k=
eep non-critical or UI state, such as "is this dropdown currently open", in=
side a component's internal state.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Some common rules for determining what kind of data should =
be put into Redux:</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Do other parts of the application needs data to be shared.</li>
<li>Is the same data being used to drive multiple components.</li>
<li>Do you want to cache the data.</li>
<li>Do you want to keep this data consistent while hot-reloading UI compone=
nts.</li>
</ul>
