<p dir=3D"auto"><code>applyMiddleware(thunk)</code>: This tells redux to ac=
cept and execute functions as return values. Redux usually only accepts obj=
ects like { type: 'ADD_THINGS', things: ['list', 'of', 'things'] }.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">The middleware checks if the action's return value is a fun=
ction and if it is it will execute the function and inject a callback funct=
ion named dispatch. This way you can start an asynchronous task and then us=
e the dispatch callback to return a regular redux object action some time i=
n the future.</p>
