<p dir=3D"auto">Any meaningful web app needs to execute complex logic, usua=
lly including asynchronous work such as making AJAX requests. That code is =
no longer purely a function of its inputs, and the interactions with the ou=
tside world are known as "side effects".</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Redux is inspired by functional programming, and out of the=
 box, has no place for side effects to be executed. In particular, reducer =
functions must always be pure functions of <code>(state, action) =3D&gt; ne=
wState</code>. However, Redux's middleware (eg. <strong>Redux Thunk</strong=
>, <strong>Redux Saga</strong>) makes it possible to intercept dispatched a=
ctions and add additional complex behavior around them, including side effe=
cts.</p>
