<p dir=3D"auto">Both Redux Thunk and Redux Saga take care of dealing with s=
ide effects. In very simple terms, applied to the most common scenario (asy=
nc functions, specifically AJAX calls) Thunk allows Promises" to deal with =
them, Saga uses Generators. Thunk is simple to use and Promises are familia=
r to many developers, Saga/Generators are more powerful but you will need t=
o learn them. When Promises are just good enough, so is Thunk, when you dea=
l with more complex cases on a regular basis, Saga gives you better tools.<=
/p>
