<p dir=3D"auto">This is a simple demonstration of how to connect all the st=
andard HTML form elements to redux-form.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">For the most part, it is a matter of wrapping each form con=
trol in a <code>&lt;Field&gt;</code> component, specifying which type of <c=
ode>React.DOM</code> component you wish to be rendered.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">The Field component will provide your input with <code>onCh=
ange</code>, <code>onBlur</code>, <code>onFocus</code>, <code>onDrag</code>=
, and <code>onDrop</code> props to listen to the events, as well as a <stro=
ng>value</strong> prop to make each input a <strong>controlled component</s=
trong>. Notice that the SimpleForm component has no state; in fact, it uses=
 the functional stateless component syntax.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
