<p dir=3D"auto"><code>createAsyncThunk</code> is a function that accepts a =
Redux action type string and a callback function that should return a promi=
se. It generates promise lifecycle action types based on the action type pr=
efix you pass in, and returns a thunk action creator that will run the prom=
ise callback and dispatch the lifecycle actions automatically.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Purpose:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Simplifies writing async logic in Redux</li>
<li>Automatically dispatches pending/fulfilled/rejected actions</li>
<li>Handles errors and loading states</li>
<li>Reduces boilerplate for async operations</li>
</ul>
