<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>1. Initializing State:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">In Redux, all application state is held in the store; which=
 is an object that holds the complete state tree of your app. There is only=
 one way to change its state and that is by dispatching actions.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Actions are objects that consist of a type and a payload pr=
operty. They are created and dispatched by special functions called action =
creators.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><em>Example: First creating the Redux store</em></p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative o=
verflow-auto" dir=3D"auto"><pre><span class=3D"pl-k">import</span> <span cl=
ass=3D"pl-kos">{</span> <span class=3D"pl-s1">createStore</span> <span clas=
s=3D"pl-kos">}</span> <span class=3D"pl-k">from</span> <span class=3D"pl-s"=
>'redux'</span>

<span class=3D"pl-k">function</span> <span class=3D"pl-en">todosReducer</sp=
