<p dir=3D"auto">Redux state functions called a reducer because it's the typ=
e of function we pass to <code>Array.prototype.reduce(reducer, ?initialValu=
e)</code>. Reducers do not just return default values. They always return t=
he accumulation of the state (based on all previous and current actions).</=
p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Therefore, they act as a reducer of state. Each time a redu=
x reducer is called, the state is passed in with the action <code>(state, a=
ction)</code>. This state is then reduced (or accumulated) based on the act=
ion, and then the next state is returned. This is one cycle of the classic =
<code>fold</code> or <code>reduce</code> function.</p>
