<p dir=3D"auto">A <strong>selector</strong> is simply a function that accep=
ts Redux state as an argument and returns data that is derived from that st=
ate.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Selectors help to keep your Redux store state minimal and d=
erive data from the state as needed. They can compute derived data, allowin=
g Redux to store the minimal possible state. Selectors are also very effici=
ent. A selector is not recomputed unless one of its arguments changes.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
